{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PATCHSET 1 -> 2: `Verified -1` triaged as a REAL failure (not a flake, not a stale base), fixed,\nre-pushed. `LLM-Review` was +1 on PS1 (PASS, 5 advisory non-blocking); both votes were cleared\nby the amend, as expected.\n\nWHAT FAILED: `build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)` — run 31568396185, one test:\n`test_proxying_transport_is_capable_and_is_not_skipped`, on\n`assert not isinstance(client, SupportsComments)`.\n\nROOT CAUSE — the hazard is VERSION-DEPENDENT and I had pinned only one side of it. The\n`getattr_static` behaviour I found locally is Python **3.12** (CPython gh-102433). CI's matrix\nruns **3.11**, where the `@runtime_checkable` check is still plain `hasattr`, so a proxying\ntransport DOES satisfy `isinstance` there. My regression test asserted 3.12 semantics\nunconditionally, so it could only ever pass on the interpreter I happened to develop on.\n\nMeasured on both interpreters in this checkout (same proxy object, same Protocol):\n\n    python3.11  hasattr add_comment=True   isinstance=True    MagicMock isinstance=True\n    python3.12  hasattr add_comment=True   isinstance=False   MagicMock isinstance=False\n\nThis makes the fallback MORE clearly load-bearing, not less: `requires-python` is `>=3.11` and\nthe project builds on both, so the SAME code runs where `isinstance` is proxy-safe and where it\nis not. A version bump is not an alternative fix. The test now asserts BOTH directions behind\n`sys.version_info >= (3, 12)` — proxy fails isinstance on 3.12+, satisfies it on 3.11 — so it is\nthe executable record of where the divergence begins and cannot silently pass by developing on\none interpreter. The behavioural assertions (the proxied write is actually CALLED, no\ncapability-absent alert, computed/applied == 1/1) stay UNCONDITIONAL on every version.\n\nWorth noting for `astute-plaster-prawn` (the ADR-0083 follow-up): this is also why the hazard\nwas invisible until now. On 3.11 an isinstance-only capability guard behaves correctly for\nproxies and MagicMocks, so ADR-0083's guidance was safe when written and silently became unsafe\nat 3.12 — a temporal-decay defect in the ADR, not an error at authoring time.\n\nRe-verified after the fix: `make lint` 0, `make typecheck` 0, `pytest tests/unit -k \"dispatch or\nreconciler\"` 2444 passed / 8 skipped. Patchset 2 pushed, same Change-Id\n`I380423010bb5bc3864de374e2f99bf236dc35bbd`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786520964594914001,"uuid":"864ddedd-9d41-4a65-ac1f-1fb1938189ff"}